{
  "id": "book-31",
  "checkpoint": 15,
  "title": "Morning at the Campfire",
  "summary": "Paul acorda com o nascer do sol no acampamento, prepara o café da manhã ao redor da fogueira e conversa sobre o tempo com uma montanhista.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-31.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Early morning light filters through the thin fabric of Paul's tent. He wakes up feeling rested, zips open the flap, and steps onto the dewy grass. A cool mist hangs over the valley below.\n\nSeveral campers gather around the embers of the fire pit. A woman named Clara is boiling water in a black kettle. “Good morning, Paul,” she greets him with a broad smile. “Would you like some hot coffee?”\n\n“Good morning, Clara. Yes, that sounds wonderful,” Paul answers gratefully.\n\nShe pours the steaming drink into a tin mug and hands it across the flames. “The mountain forecast looks clear today, but high winds often strike the eastern ridge by noon.”\n\nPaul takes a sip and checks his compass. “I plan to ascend early to avoid the wind.”\n\nClara nods approvingly as they finish their breakfast together.",
